        <div id="warranty" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Warranty: What Precor Covers and What the Seller Covers</h2>
<p>
            Precor publishes different warranties for the same treadmill depending on where it is used, and none
            of them passes to a second owner. That is the single biggest difference between a new and a rebuilt
            Precor’s real cost.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Cover</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">New, sold into a home</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">New, commercial use</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Rebuilt (typical)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Frame</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lifetime</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">7 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Seller’s term only</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Parts, including belt, deck and drive motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3 years (motor 5)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1 year (Fitness Superstore, Build A Gym, Global Fitness refurbished)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Console</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3 years</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Seller’s term (usually within the 1-year parts cover)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Labour</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1 year</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">3 years from 30 March 2026</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">1 year (on-site at Fitness Superstore)</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The home column is Precor’s “Commercial Cardio Equipment Sold Into Residential (Home)” limited warranty
            and the commercial column its Limited Standard Warranty summary for the 800, 700, 600 and 500 lines,
            both linked from Precor’s US warranty page on 27 November 2026. The summary says that from 30 March 2026
            commercial buyers get three years of labour, but that “Commercial units sold in to a home remain covered
            by a one (1) year labor warranty”, and that parts on 600-line products made after 16 July 2021 are
            limited to three years in the US and Canada.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The conditions that change the value</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Original buyer only.</strong> The home warranty “extends only to the original purchaser” and
            says, in capitals, that it “IS NOT ASSIGNABLE AND CANNOT BE RE-SOLD”. A used Precor has no Precor cover.</li>
            <li><strong>The clock may already be running.</strong> Cover starts on the invoice date or one year after
            Precor shipped the unit to the dealer, whichever comes first. Ask for the ship date.</li>
            <li><strong>Home use only.</strong> It excludes membership facilities, corporate wellness, multi-family
            housing, hotels and personal training studios.</li>
            <li><strong>Wear and console items.</strong> Normal wear and tear is excluded, and high-wear console items
            such as headphone jacks and USB connectors get 90 days.</li>
          </ul>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What longer cover costs on a rebuilt Precor</h3>
          <p>
            Fitness Superstore’s TRM 885 V2 page priced its extended options on 27 November 2026 at $299, $624, $924
            and $1,249 for two to five years of residential parts and labour, and $424 to $1,749 for two to five years
            of commercial cover. Top Fitness’s refurbished TRM 885 already comes with three years of parts and three of
            labour, which is the longest included term we saw. On a $4,000 rebuilt treadmill, a two-year residential
            plan at $299 is about 7% of the price; whether it is worth it depends on how far you are from a technician.
            Our <a href="/treadmill-warranty-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill warranty guide</a> explains how to read these terms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="delivery" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Delivery, Installation and the 20-Amp Circuit</h2>
<p>
            A Precor club <a href="/how-much-does-a-treadmill-weigh/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>treadmill weighs</a> roughly 385 to 430 lb, does not fold and usually arrives mostly or fully
            assembled, so getting it into a room is part of the price. These are the delivery options published on
            27 November 2026.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[600px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Seller</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Kerbside</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Into the room</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Lead time stated</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Top Fitness, new</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Free (“Economy”)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$399 delivery and assembly in room of choice, including stairs</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Ships in 4+ weeks; home delivery typically 6+ weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Top Fitness, refurbished TRM 885</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$499</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$899</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Delivery typically 2–4 weeks</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Fitness Superstore, rebuilt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$0 kerbside; $100 garage, left in crate</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$349 garage install; $449 room of choice (0–3 steps); $599 stair carry (4+ steps)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Ships from warehouse in 3–5 weeks plus transit</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Build A Gym, rebuilt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Driveway freight, priced by ZIP</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Inside delivery and assembly, priced by ZIP</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">“Receive by Dec 25” estimate</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Global Fitness</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Priced at checkout by ZIP</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Not stated on the product page</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">“Most products ship within 24 hours”</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            So the landed price of a new TRM 885 (P84) from Top Fitness, carried in and assembled, was $16,024
            before tax. A Fitness Superstore TRM 885 V2 placed in a ground-floor room was $4,448 ($3,999 plus $449),
            or $4,248.05 with the BF5 code taken off the machine. A Top Fitness refurbished TRM 885 brought in was
            $4,598. Build A Gym’s and Global Fitness’s delivery charges depend on your ZIP code, so get them before
            comparing their lower machine prices.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The circuit can cost more than the delivery</h3>
          <p>
            Top Fitness’s TRM 885 page states that the treadmill “requires a dedicated 120V/20A circuit with a 5-20R
            NEMA receptacle to operate in a home. GFCI outlets are not supported.” That matches Precor’s brochures for
            the TRM 600, 700 and 800 lines. Its TRM 531 page gives 120V/15A with a NEMA 5-20 receptacle, the same
            conflict our Precor guide found in Precor’s own documents for the 500 line. Build A Gym’s pages for its
            rebuilt TRM 835, 833 and 865 say the opposite: “Standard household outlet, no dedicated 20A circuit
            needed, adapter included.” We cannot reconcile those. Follow the installation manual for the exact model
            and serial number, ask the seller to put its power advice in writing, and have an electrician check the
            circuit before delivery. We found no dated published price for adding a circuit, so get a local quote.
            Precor’s home warranty excludes damage from wiring that does not meet codes or the owner’s manual. Our <a href="/gym-treadmill-for-home/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide to putting a gym treadmill in a home</a> covers access and floor
            loading.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="parts-repair" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Parts and Repair Costs</h2>
<p>
            Precor’s popularity in gyms keeps parts easy to find. These are third-party part listings on Amazon on
            27 November 2026; most are sold as compatible with named Precor models rather than as Precor-branded
            parts, so match the part number and serial number range to your machine before ordering.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[580px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Part</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Example listing</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Amazon price (27 Nov)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Walking (running) belt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">TRM 885 2-ply belt, by serial prefix; generic Precor commercial 2-ply belt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$158.85–$209.99</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Motor drive belt</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">TRM 885, by serial prefix</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$78.99</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline (lift) motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Precor 9.2x, 9.3x and C932i models, by part number</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$76.99–$203.99</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">DC drive motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">From 9.4x home-model motors to TRM 631/661/681 and other club motors</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$177.09–$599.99</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Lower motor control board</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Precor 9.2x, 9.21s and TRM 211 boards</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$102.89–$467.89</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Deck cushion</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Precor part PPP000000044236101</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$37.79</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            Labour is the larger number. Our <a href="/treadmill-motor-replacement-cost/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">motor replacement cost guide</a> recorded a certified-technician first visit at $269.99 and one regional repairer’s $185 diagnosis and
            labour charge in November 2026, and found Precor drive motors on Amazon from $293.99 to $719.99. Precor’s
            home warranty covers only one year of labour, so from year two a ten-year part still needs a paid visit.
            On a rebuilt machine with a one-year warranty, a lift motor replaced in year two would come to roughly
            $260 to $475 on these figures ($76.99 to $203.99 for the part plus $185 to $269.99 for the visit), so a
            two-year extended plan at $299 is priced close to one such repair.
          </p>
          <p>
            The dealer guide cited in our Precor page names the incline motor as the most common failure on used
            Precors, followed by drive motors and controllers on older units, belts and decks where lubrication was
            neglected, and touchscreens on the older P80 console. Precor’s summary says post-warranty support for
            discontinued products “may be available for up to 7 years beyond the last date of manufacture”, so parts
            for a C956i or Premium Series machine are third-party parts, not factory stock.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="vs-others" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Precor vs Life Fitness, Matrix and Landice at the Same Tier</h2>
<p>
            At the rebuilt-club tier the brands cost almost the same; at the new tier they differ a great deal,
            mainly because Precor has no home range. These are the prices recorded on this site, with dates.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[660px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Brand</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Rebuilt club treadmill</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">New, sold for homes</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">New club treadmill</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Precor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">TRM 885 $3,799–$4,799; TRM 835 $2,495–$3,999 (27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">No home range; TRM 531 from $5,885 via a dealer (Top Fitness, 27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">TRM 835 $11,860 to TRM 895 $16,230 (Top Fitness, 27 Nov 2026)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Life Fitness</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">95T $3,799–$4,099; Integrity SE3 HD $5,199 (Fitness Superstore, 27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Run CX $4,899 (Life Fitness, 14 Oct 2026); Club Series+ $6,079, compare at $10,999 (The Fitness Outlet, 27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Integrity+ SL $11,247 (facility store, Nov 2026)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Matrix</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T3x $3,799; T5x $3,799–$4,099; T7xi $4,499 (Fitness Superstore, 27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">T30 to T75, $4,699–$7,399 (Matrix home store, October 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">“Call for pricing” at dealers (Nov 2026)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Landice</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">L7 Pro Sports Trainer and L9 $3,799 (Fitness Superstore, 27 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">L7 $5,429–$7,804 by configuration (Landice, 5 Nov 2026)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Sold as the same L-series; no separate club line priced</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            <strong>Rebuilt:</strong> Fitness Superstore priced most rebuilt club treadmills from all four brands at
            $3,799 to $4,099, with the same one-year parts and on-site labour warranty. At that tier, choose on the
            unit’s generation and console, the seller’s warranty and how close a technician is, not the badge. Precor’s
            edge is that more of them circulate, so parts and technicians are easy to find.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>New:</strong> a buyer who wants a new club-quality treadmill with a home warranty and a published
            price has cheaper options than a new Precor. The Life Fitness <a href="/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Run CX</a> was $4,899 on Life Fitness’s store in October and a new Club Series+ $6,079 at The
            Fitness Outlet on Black Friday, the Matrix home range starts at $4,699, and a Landice L7 starts at $5,429. A new
            TRM 531 at $5,885 is the cheapest new Precor, and it is Precor’s light-commercial line with a 350 lb
            rating. A new TRM 885 at $14,640 to $15,625 is a facility purchase. See our <a href="/commercial-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">commercial-grade treadmills</a> roundup for home-buyable alternatives and
            our <a href="/landice-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Landice guide</a> for the built-to-order option.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="who-should-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Who Should Buy New, Who Should Buy Rebuilt</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Buy a rebuilt Precor if</strong> you want a club treadmill for heavy daily use at a home-treadmill
            price, you can confirm the power and the route into the room, and the seller gives a written warranty of
            at least a year with on-site labour. On 27 November 2026 that meant about $3,800 to $4,800 for a TRM 885
            or 781, or $2,500 to $4,000 for a TRM 835, plus $0 to $899 to get it inside.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Buy a used, as-is Precor if</strong> the price reflects 30 days of cover or none, you have seen it
            run through the full incline range at your speed, and a local technician confirms parts. Global Fitness’s
            used TRM 731 at $1,645 shows how low a sold-in-working-order Precor can go; budget a technician visit in
            year one.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Buy a new Precor if</strong> you specifically want the current 800 line’s 16 mph top speed and
            decline (Precor’s figures), a current P84 or P94 console, a lifetime frame and ten-year parts warranty in
            your own name, or you are equipping a building’s gym. Get the ship date, the home warranty and the power
            requirement in writing.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Buy something else if</strong> your budget is under about $2,500, you need a folding frame or a
            15-amp plug with no doubt about it, or you want a big Black Friday discount. Home brands that discount
            hard this week, and rebuilt Life Fitness, Matrix or Landice machines at the same $3,799, are all worth a
            look before you commit. Our <a href="/refurbished-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">refurbished treadmills guide</a> lists the questions to ask any rebuilder.
          </p>
        </div>


        <!-- Common mistakes -->
        <div id="common-mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Where People Go Wrong When Pricing a Precor Treadmill</h2>
          <p>Precor’s prices are spread across dealers and rebuilders. These are the mistakes that cost buyers most.</p>
          <ol class="ed-mistakes not-prose">
            <li>
              <h3>Comparing a rebuilt TRM 885 with a new one as if they were the same</h3>
              <p>Rebuilt TRM 885s carry P80 or P82 consoles and “V1” or “V2” labels; the current model has the P84. Compare like with like: on 27 November the P82 TRM 885 was $14,640 new and $4,799 rebuilt. Ask for a photo of the serial label and console.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Trusting a listing’s warranty bullet</h3>
              <p>Old Amazon listings still say “Lifetime warranty on frame and welds, 10-years on parts”. That is Precor’s original-buyer warranty, which cannot be resold. Ask the seller what cover it gives, in writing, and price the machine on that.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Ignoring delivery and power until the truck arrives</h3>
              <p>Getting a 400 lb treadmill into a room cost $399 to $899 at the sellers we read, and Precor specifies a dedicated 20-amp circuit for its TRM 600 to 800 lines. Price both before you compare machine prices, and have an electrician check the circuit first.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <h3>Chasing the Black Friday code instead of the cheapest seller</h3>
              <p>The codes were worth 5 to 10%, roughly $190 to $280 on a Precor. The same TRM 835 was $2,495 at one rebuilder and $3,999 at another. Compare the model, console, warranty and landed price across sellers, then apply the code.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- The bottom line -->
        <div id="bottom-line" class="ed-bottomline">
          <h2>The bottom line</h2>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">A Precor treadmill costs $5,885 to $16,230 new and about $2,500 to $4,800 rebuilt.</strong> On 27 November 2026 an authorized dealer listed the TRM 531 at $5,885 and the TRM 885 at $14,640 to $15,625,
            while rebuilders sold the TRM 835 from $2,495 and the TRM 885 from $3,799 with a one-year warranty. Precor
            itself publishes no prices and sells no home treadmill.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong class="text-white">For most homes, a rebuilt Precor is the one that makes sense.</strong> It costs about
            a third of new, and Precor’s own warranty would not pass to you second-hand anyway. Add $0 to $899 for
            delivery, confirm the circuit in writing, and compare sellers before codes. Our <a href="/precor-treadmills/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Precor treadmill guide</a> covers the models and the checks to make before you buy.
          </p>
        </div>

