        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much is a new Precor treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Precor publishes no prices. Top Fitness, an authorized Precor distributor, listed new Precor treadmills from $5,885 (TRM 531) to $16,230 (TRM 895 with the P94 console) on 27 November 2026. A new TRM 885 was $14,640 with the P82 console and $15,625 with the P84.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a used Precor treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On 27 November 2026, remanufactured Precors with a one-year warranty were $2,495 (TRM 835, Build A Gym) to $4,799 (TRM 885 with P82, Fitness Superstore). Global Fitness sold used units in working order from $1,375 for a C932i to $3,575 for a TRM 885, with 30 days of parts-only cover.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much does a Precor TRM 885 cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              New, $14,640 with the P82 console or $15,625 with the P84 at Top Fitness on 27 November 2026. Rebuilt, $3,799 to $4,799 at Fitness Superstore depending on generation and console, $3,699 refurbished at Top Fitness and $3,975 refurbished at Global Fitness. Amazon showed a P80-console listing at $3,495 with no condition stated.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Precor make a home treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not one you can buy new. Precor At Home listed 13 products on 27 November 2026 and no treadmill. Precor’s warranty summary still lists 200 and 400 Series home lines, but we found neither on sale. Dealers sell the commercial TRM models into homes with a separate home warranty.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is there a Precor Black Friday sale?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not from Precor. On 27 November 2026 Fitness Superstore offered 5% off remanufactured equipment with code BF5 until 30 November, and Build A Gym 10% off remanufactured equipment with code JACKEDFRIDAY, ending 3 December. Top Fitness showed no sale price on new Precor treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does the Precor warranty transfer to a second owner?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              No. Precor’s warranty for commercial equipment sold into a home covers the original purchaser only and states it is not assignable and cannot be resold. A used or rebuilt Precor relies on the seller’s own warranty, typically one year of parts and labour.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a remanufactured Precor worth it?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Often, for heavy home use. A rebuilt TRM 885 or 781 cost about a third of the same model new on 27 November 2026, with a one-year parts and on-site labour warranty. Check the power requirement, the console generation and the delivery cost to your room first.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
